🔥 REACT.JS – HARD INTERVIEW QUESTIONS & ANSWERS (CORE → ADVANCED)
🧠 SECTION 1: CORE FUNDAMENTALS
1️⃣ What is React?
React is a JavaScript library for building fast, interactive UI using components and Virtual DOM.

2️⃣ Why React is fast?
Because it uses Virtual DOM + efficient diffing + reconciliation, reducing real DOM updates.

3️⃣ What is Virtual DOM?
A lightweight JavaScript copy of the real DOM used to calculate minimal UI updates.

4️⃣ SPA vs MPA?
SPA	MPA
Single page	Multiple pages
Fast	Slow
React	Traditional sites
5️⃣ What is JSX?
JSX is a syntax extension that lets us write HTML inside JavaScript.

🧩 SECTION 2: COMPONENTS & STATE
6️⃣ What is a component?
Reusable UI block that returns JSX.

7️⃣ Functional vs Class components?
Functional components use hooks and are simpler. Class components are older.

8️⃣ What are props?
Props are read-only data passed from parent to child.

9️⃣ What is state?
State is mutable data that controls component behavior and UI.

🔟 Why state changes re-render UI?
Because React compares old and new Virtual DOM and updates changes.

🎣 SECTION 3: HOOKS (MOST ASKED)
11️⃣ What are hooks?
Functions that let functional components use React features.

12️⃣ Rules of hooks?
Only call hooks at top level

Only inside React functions

13️⃣ useState?
Manages component-level state.

14️⃣ useEffect?
Handles side effects (API calls, subscriptions).

15️⃣ useEffect dependency array?
[] → once

[x] → on x change

no array → every render

16️⃣ Cleanup in useEffect?
Used to remove listeners, timers.

return () => clearInterval(id);
17️⃣ useRef?
Access DOM

Store mutable values without re-render

18️⃣ useContext?
Avoids prop drilling by sharing global data.

19️⃣ useMemo?
Caches expensive calculations.

20️⃣ useCallback?
Caches function references to prevent re-creation.

